Swami Vivekananda wanted to create such youths who have love and trust in each other without any discrimination.
A youth is one who works towards his future goals without worrying about the past.
The work that all of you youngsters do today becomes the future of the country.
Friends, today the age of more than 80 crore people in the country is below 35 years.
Today, India has the ability to usher in an era that can become a world guru by following the path set by Swami Vivekananda.
Today, this land of Haryana is also a great inspiration for my young friends who are in Rohtak at the moment.
This land of Haryana belongs to the Vedas, to the Upanishads, to the Gita.
This is the work of the brave heroes, Jai Jawan - Jai is the land of the farmer.
This is the holy house of Saraswati.
Constant effort to move forward by saving your culture, your values, can be learned from this earth.
I am happy that this time the National Youth Festival is THEME- YOUTH FOR DIGITAL INDIA….
Through this festival, youth will be imparted training in digital transactions in everyday life.
I appeal to every youth taking training in this festival to teach digital transactions to at least 10 families around them when they take training from here.
All of you youth have a big role to play in making LESSCASH economy.
This will be an important contribution of you in the fight to free the country from black money and corruption.
This year, the National Youth Festival has been chosen as the daughter of Shubhankar.
"It is named as ""Mhari Lado"" from Dular."
"The effort to raise awareness about the ""Beti Bachao - Beti Padhao"" campaign through this festival is highly appreciated."
"It was from Haryana itself that the Central Government started the ""Beti Bachao - Beti Padhao"" campaign."
This campaign is seeing a big impact in this area.
Change has begun.
The SEX RATIO has changed significantly.
This change is increasing for the whole country.
I especially congratulate the people of Haryana for this.
This shows that when people are determined, the impossible becomes possible.
I hope that soon Haryana will show a proud state for the entire country by building.
The youth class is playing a big role in shaping the future of Haryana.
The young players of Haryana have always raised the value of the entire country by winning medals in many international events.
There is a need for more contribution of youth power to touch new heights of development across the country.
India's goal is to provide its youth with the capabilities and skills to make this century India's century.
Friends, the National Youth Festival provides a platform for all of you to showcase your talent.
All of you young people coming from different cultural surroundings will get a chance to understand knowing each other here.
This is the true meaning of one Bharat-Shrestha Bharat.
Just a little while ago, the march past of cultural parties of all states and union territories has been taken out at the Youth Festival.
An India-superior India is an attempt to unify the cultural diversity of the country.
In our country, languages ​​may be different, food and food are different, the way of living is different, the customs are different, but the soul is the same.
The name of that soul is - Indianness.
And we and all of us are proud for this Indianness.
If the youth of one state meets the youth of another state, they will also have a new experience, respect for each other will increase, understanding will increase.
When people live together, they understand that these food and linguistic differences are superficial.
Looking deeply, it is clear that our values, our humanity, our philosophy are the same.
Friends, under one Bharat-Shrestha Bharat, two different states have been partnered for a year.
This year, Haryana has partnered with Telangana. Action points have also been created for which subjects will be mutually supported in the two states.
I hope that today students from Telangana in Haryana will get to know a lot especially.
An India-superior India is not just a plan.
It is being carried forward like a mass movement and it will be successful only when the youth of the country will get full support.
My young friends, this year the country is celebrating the centenary of Pandit Deen Dayal Upadhyay.
Panditji's mantra for the youth of the country was - Charaivati-Charaivati, Charaivati, keep walking, keep walking, do not stop, do not stop, go on the path of nation building.
In this era of technology, the youth of the country today have to focus on the Three C’s. When I speak of Three C’s I mean first C COLLECTIVITY, second C CONNECTIVITY and third C CREATIVITY….
COLLECTIVITY COLLABORATION Until we become an organized power, we do not gather Indians by erasing discrimination, COLLECTIVITY strength is a very big force.
Second thing is CONNECTIVITY country era has changed.
Technology has made the whole world very small.
The whole world is in your palm in your hand.
CONNECTIVITY is the demand of time.
We will continue to emphasize our human values ​​along with technology from CONNECTIVITY point of view.
And thirdly, I said CREATIVITY new ideas, new INNOVATION, new ways to solve old problems, and this is what is expected from the youth.
At which CREATIVITY ends.
INNOVATION runs out.
Newness gets stuck in a way life stops.
And that's why we should continue to give as much opportunity to the CREATIVITY within us.
So contact each other, learn to take collective responsibility and work on new ideas.
Do not let your new ideas end by thinking that they are too small or what other people will say.
Remember that most of the big and new ideas in the world have already been rejected.
Whatever the existing system is, it opposes new ideas.
But I am sure that every such protest will cool down in front of the youth power of our country.
Friends, speaking on Integral Humanism more than fifty years ago, what Pandit Deen Dayal Upadhyay had said, also has a big message for the youth of the country.
Deen Dayal Upadhyay Ji called for nation building and fighting the evils present in the country.
They said-
We have to end many stereotypes.
We will do what is necessary in the development of our human and the growth of unity of the nation, and we will remove whatever is hindering us.
In the body God has given, there is no need to take out Meenmakh or walk with self-sacrifice.
But if there is an abscess in the body, its operation is necessary.
No need to cut living and healthy organs.
Today if untouchability and discrimination in the society have become home, due to which people do not think of humans as human and which are proving fatal to the unity of the nation, we will eliminate them.
This call of Pandit ji is equally important today.
Even today there is untouchability, corruption, black money, illiteracy, malnutrition.
To eliminate all these evils, the youth of the country must exert their power.
Just a few days ago, the government has taken major action against black money and corruption.
The support given by my young friends to this action is a proof of the tremendous will among all of you to eradicate the evil prevailing in the society.
So when I say my country is changing, your efforts are behind it.
Thousands of millions of youth in different parts of the country are fighting their own social evils and challenges.
Not only this, he is bringing such new ideas that I could not live without bowing to him.
Just a few days ago in Mann Ki Baat I mentioned a girl who gave the idea that mango trees would be given to guests at the wedding as a return gift. What a wonderful way to save the environment.
Similarly, people in one area were deeply troubled by the lack of garbage. In such a situation, the youth of the area combined the garbage containers with advertising.
Now on the streets there, you will see garbage cans everywhere, which will also be advertised.
In our country, such youth full of energy are present in every corner. Some are making electricity from small springs coming out of the mountains, some are constructing houses with garbage, some are providing medical facilities in remote areas through technology, some are providing water to farmers in drought-prone areas Is gathering resources to save.
Millions of such youth are doing day and night for nation building.
For every such energetic youth, I would like to repeat Swami Vivekananda's message again.
Wake up, wake up and don't stop until the goal is achieved.
Rise means to enlighten the body, make the body energetic, keep the body fit. Many times it has been seen that people get up but do not wake up.
Because of this, they are unable to assess the situation correctly.
Therefore it is necessary to be awake as you get up.
When it is not decided where to go, then how it will be able to decide in which direction and where to go.
So when the goal is set, then try to achieve it without stopping, without wearying.
My friends, all of you are present in front of me as intellectual strength of the country.
Today it is necessary to protect the youth from being paranoid.
Today there is a need to keep the youth away from drugs and crime.
You create a new way by thinking and brainstorming, get new floors.
There is an open sky of possibilities in front of you.
There is a need today that the youth become unmatched examples of service.
There should be honesty and fairness in his character.
Have the courage to face every challenge.
May he be proud of his glorious heritage.
Their behavior and character should be based on moral values.
I am stressing this because the harder it is to achieve the goal, the easier it is to deviate from the goal.
Criticizing the opposition, the Prime Minister said, these are the people who used to raise questions about PM Kisan Samman Nidhi, spreading the rumor that this money is being given in view of the elections and after the election the same money will have to be given back with interest.
He added that in a state, where the opposition government is there, due to its political interest, farmers are not allowed to take advantage of this scheme.
He said assistance is being provided directly to the bank accounts of more than 10 crore farmer families of the country.
So far, about 1 lakh crore rupees have been reached the farmers.
The Prime Minister said decades of deceit make farmers apprehensive but now there is no deceit, work is being done with intentions as pure as Gangajal.
He remarked that the truth of those who spread illusions on the basis of mere apprehensions is being constantly exposed before the country.
When farmers understand their lies, then they start spreading lies on another subject.
He added the government is also constantly answering those farmer families who still have some concerns.
He expressed confidence that those farmers who have some doubts on agricultural reforms today, will also take advantage of these agricultural reforms in future and increase their income.
PM interacts with three teams working on developing & manufacturing COVID-19 vaccine
The Prime Minister on Monday had virtual meetings with 3 teams working on developing & manufacturing vaccine for COVID-19.
These teams were from Gennova Biopharmaceuticals Ltd Pune, Biological E Ltd Hyderabad and Dr. Reddys Laboratories Ltd Hyderabad.
The PM appreciated the efforts being taken by the scientists in these companies to come out with a vaccine solution to tackle COVID-19.
The potential of various platforms for vaccine development was also discussed.
PM also asked the companies to come out with their suggestions and ideas regarding the regulatory processes and related matters.
He also suggested that they should take extra efforts to inform the general public in simple language about the vaccine and related matters such as its efficacy etc.
Matters relating to logistics, transport, cold chain etc in respect of delivering the vaccines were also discussed.
All the vaccine candidates discussed are at different stages of trials and detailed data and results are expected early next year onwards.
The PM advised all the departments concerned to engage with the manufacturers and seek to resolve matters so that the efforts by these companies bear fruit in order to serve the needs of the country and the entire world.
PM greets people on Parkash Purab of Guru Nanak
The Prime Minister, Shri Narendra Modi has greeted the people on the occasion of Parkash Purab of Shri Guru Nanak Dev Ji.
In a tweet, the Prime Minister said, I bow to Sri Guru Nanak Dev Ji on his Parkash Purab.
May his thoughts keep motivating us to serve society and ensure a better planet.
PM condoles the passing away of Rajya Sabha MP Shri Abhay Bharadwaj
The Prime Minister, Shri Narendra Modi has expressed grief over the demise of Rajya Sabha MP from Gujarat, Shri Abhay Bharadwaj.
In a tweet, the Prime Minister said, Rajya Sabha MP from Gujarat, Shri Abhay Bharadwaj Ji was a distinguished lawyer and remained at the forefront of serving society.
It is sad we have lost a bright and insightful mind, passionate about national development.
Condolences to his family and friends.
Om Shanti.
