The North East Regional Institute of Education
Introduction
The North East Regional Institute of Education (NERIE) stands amidst the natural grandeur in Umiam village, which is about 20 kms away from Shillong city.
Like other constituent units of the National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT), New Delhi, this Regional Institute of Education too, caters to the educational needs of the eight states of the North East- Assam, Arunachal Pradesh, Manipur, Meghalaya, Mizoram, Nagaland, Sikkim and Tripura.
Its history dates back to the year 1992, when the 'Task force' of the NCERT headed by Madhuri Shah recommended for the setting up a Regional College for the NCERT in the North East.
The first step taken in this regard, was in the year 1995, when the then Field Units of the NCERT at Guwahati and Shillong were amalgamated into one to form the North East Regional Institute of Education at Shillong.
At that time, Prof C.L Anand, the then Vice Chancellor of Arunachal University, was instrumental in preparing the blue print to set up the Institute.
The NERIE continued to function as a Field Office for about ten years.
However, in the year 2005, the post of Principal along with 24 posts for the faculty were advertised and filled up by the NCERT, New Delhi.
The increase in the faculty strength led to an increase in the number of administerial staff in the Institute.
As the Institute's human power was growing, the Institute in May 2012 had to be shifted from Shillong to its permanent campus in Nongsder village, Umiam.
The building was inaugurated by the then Hon'ble Minister of Human Resource Development, Government of India Dr. MM Pahalam Raju, Deputy Chief Minister of Meghalaya and Education Minister Prof. RC Lalu as the Honorary Guest along with several dignitaries, Shri Rajshree Bhattacharya, Indian Administrative Services, Ministry of Human Resource Development, Government of India, Professor Parveen Sinclair, Former Director, NCERT, New Delhi and Professor A. Sukmar, former Principal of the Institute, teachers, staff and other guests on 07th June, 2013.
In sync with the NCERT's objectives, the objectives of the Institute are spelled out as follows-
(I) To undertake, aid, promote and coordinate research in all branches of education. - As such in a year, the Institute carries out on an average eight research programmes.
"(II) To conduct pre- service training courses in the region- The Institute reached one of its milestones in the year 2015, when the Two year B.Ed course was launched.
("
III) To organize in- service training programmes based on the educational needs of the eight states- On an average per academic session, the Institute conducts as many as twenty to twenty five training programmes.
(IV) To develop educational materials, learning resources for both students and teachers as per the needs of the time and age-About ten such programmes are conducted every year.
(V) To organize extension services- This is done mainly through seminars and conferences at regional and national level.
The sole purpose is to make the Institute a learning space in recent trends in school education and teacher education.
(VI) To provide leadership in training, development and research activities on the flagship programmes of the Ministry of Human Resource and Development (MHRD), GOI.
In these past years, the Institute took the lead in the implementation of the Sarva Shiksha Abhiyan and Rastriya Madhyamik Shiksha Abhiyan programmes for the universalization of school education in the country.
From this academic year onwards, the Institute will take up programmes on the Samagra Shiksha Abhiyan, the newly launched programme of MHRD.
NERIE Campus
North East Regional Institute of Education is located at NERIE Campus, Umiam, Ri-Bhoi District, Meghalaya-793103.
The residential campus for NERIE has been constructed by the Central Public Works Department (CPWD) at Barapani near Shillong amidst the picturesque hills of the East Khasi Hills of Meghalaya.
The campus is located 2 Kms off from the Guwahati-Shillong highway and about 20 Kms from Police Bazar, Shillong.
The geographical location of this Institute is 25.672790 (Latitude) and 91.914061 (Longitude).
This new campus is next to North East Space Application Centre (NESAC), ISRO.
The campus is having a well-furnished administrative building (having space for office and faculty, conference rooms, library, EDUSAT, computer laboratory, Studio for e-content development, Photography, Videography and teleconferencing),auditorium, guest house and residential premises with housing facilities for the Principal, faculty and staffs.
The entire campus is Wifi enabled.
Besides this the Institute have other Facilities as mentioned below:
QUARTERS:
1. Principal Bungalow
2. Type-V
3. Type-IV
4. Type-III
5. Type-II
6. Type-I
Sports Facilities:
1. Table Tennis
2. Volleyball
3. Badminton
4. Cricket/Football - MeCL ground is used.
SALES COUNTER
Sales counter of North East Regional Institute of Education is located at NERIE Campus, Umiam, Ri-Bhoi District, Meghalaya-793103.
The Sales Counter main purpose is for selling NCERT Publication to individuals and Institutions.
This Sale Counter is run by the Institute under the overall supervision of the Principal.
The sale counter deals with NCERT Books i.e. from Class I-XII, and other NCERT general publications in which the lists of Books for purchase from the sales counter is displayed in the Institute Official website (http://www.nerie.nic.in/library.html).
The mode of payment is cash only in which receipt/cash memo will be issued on every purchase of Books.
The Sales Counter opens from Monday-Friday(Timing-9:00AM-4.00PM) excluding holidays as per Central Government notifications.
For any information and queries, please contact.
North East Regional Institute of Education (NERIE), NCERT
Umiam, Barapani, Shillong-793103 Meghalaya.
