DIGITAL LIBRARY
Sahitya Sagar
Projects & Schemes
The Two Projects running successfully under Sahitya Akademi are:-
Archives of Indian Literature
Centres for Translation
The Four schemes running successfully under the guidance of Sahitya Akademi are:-
Encyclopaedia of Indian Poetics
Navodya Scheme
National Bibliography of Indian Literature
History of Indian Literature
Archives of Indian Literature -
In a country that has since time immemorial largely relied on the oral tradition for dissemination of knowledge and information, lack of concern for documentation may seem natural.
Yet in this age of information, this callousness seems more and more unpardonable.
Keeping in view the importance and need of recording in the field of literature, Sahitya Akademi started a project of Archives of Indian Literature from March 1997.
Archives have been created to collect and preserve important material related to authors and literature, such as manuscripts, pictures, audio recordings, video recordings and portraits etc.
By aggregating video films and footage, manuscripts of authors, interesting correspondence and interviews between authors and audio recordings of texts available with institutions and individuals across India, it will form a solid foundation for a museum of Indian literature.
In addition, the project aims to popularize authors, texts and traditions by publishing memento forms of posters and picture postcards.
It can also advise the central and state governments and literary institutions to preserve the archive monuments.
Under this project, workshops will be organized on the methods of film-making on writers and the techniques of authors' films and the methods of archival-related records and preservation of literary monuments.
Sahitya Akademi has started work on the project of archives of films and video recordings of Indian authors and their writings.
The archives of films, images, voices, important life events that changed their lives, contemporary responses to their thoughts and creative achievements made by the Akademi on important Indian writers will be the seed of the unique Indian Literary Museum of the future, which will serve the common readers and will be useful to literary researchers and historians.
These films have been produced by directors who are creative artists of their kind.
The Akademi has so far produced video films on the following authors:
